WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.627 --> 00:00:01.687
(upbeat music)

00:00:01.687 --> 00:00:04.961
- You can have a regular normal
body guy with his shirt off

00:00:04.961 --> 00:00:05.794
trying to inspire people,

00:00:05.794 --> 00:00:07.210
or you can have me,

00:00:07.210 --> 00:00:09.793
a guy with no legs and one arm.

00:00:14.361 --> 00:00:16.031
(somber music)

00:00:16.031 --> 00:00:17.234
My name's Nick Santonastasso,

00:00:17.234 --> 00:00:19.079
I have Hanhart Syndrome,

00:00:19.079 --> 00:00:21.151
and Hanhart Syndrome
is a rare genetic disorder

00:00:21.151 --> 00:00:23.632
which either leaves the
baby with undeveloped limbs

00:00:23.632 --> 00:00:25.200
or undeveloped organs.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.505
In my case, it was just
my limbs that were,

00:00:27.505 --> 00:00:29.142
you know, affected.

00:00:29.142 --> 00:00:31.449
Middle school was like my rock bottom.

00:00:31.449 --> 00:00:32.609
I was always asking, you know,

00:00:32.609 --> 00:00:33.971
why was I born like this?

00:00:33.971 --> 00:00:36.162
Had suicidal thoughts.

00:00:36.162 --> 00:00:41.003
Wrestling started me on, you
know, the answer to why.

00:00:41.003 --> 00:00:43.279
I had to have standing
ovations when I lost,

00:00:43.279 --> 00:00:44.356
and I just didn't understand

00:00:44.356 --> 00:00:46.005
because I'm a very competitive person,

00:00:46.005 --> 00:00:47.441
I'm like, you're not supposed to cheer on

00:00:47.441 --> 00:00:49.819
someone that loses.

00:00:49.819 --> 00:00:51.691
After the matches, I'd
have parents come up to me

00:00:51.691 --> 00:00:52.524
and be like hey,

00:00:52.524 --> 00:00:53.953
my kid never did a sport,

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:55.575
and he saw you today,
and now he's signed up

00:00:55.575 --> 00:00:56.710
for all these sports, you know,

00:00:56.710 --> 00:00:58.550
because he sees that if you're doing it,

00:00:58.550 --> 00:01:00.654
there's no excuse for him not to.

00:01:00.654 --> 00:01:04.103
It was like, that's why I'm here,

00:01:04.103 --> 00:01:06.307
and I wanted to break
into the fitness industry,

00:01:06.307 --> 00:01:09.180
because I was inspired
by these fitness guys

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:11.964
that, you know, sit around
with their six pack

00:01:11.964 --> 00:01:13.309
next to their nice car,

00:01:13.309 --> 00:01:16.283
but getting into it,
it's much more than that,

00:01:16.283 --> 00:01:18.460
it's how you can move people and show them

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:20.954
that, like, living a healthy
lifestyle is not as hard

00:01:20.954 --> 00:01:21.787
as you think it is,

00:01:21.787 --> 00:01:23.954
especially if I can do it.

00:01:25.114 --> 00:01:26.232
My life revolves around, you know,

00:01:26.232 --> 00:01:28.958
eating and training and posting.

00:01:28.958 --> 00:01:30.740
(camera flashes)

00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:31.637
I look at being fit,

00:01:31.637 --> 00:01:34.363
I look at motivating
and inspiring as a duty.

00:01:34.363 --> 00:01:36.540
I got a message from a UK mom,

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:39.873
she had twins and one of the
twin’s legs had to be amputated,

00:01:39.873 --> 00:01:42.249
she said that they watched the videos together

00:01:42.249 --> 00:01:43.574
and he goes, like me, mom,

00:01:43.574 --> 00:01:44.954
he's like me, mom.

00:01:44.954 --> 00:01:46.141
I didn't have that as a kid,

00:01:46.141 --> 00:01:47.491
I didn't have someone to look up to.

00:01:47.491 --> 00:01:49.347
That kid can you know, oh,

00:01:49.347 --> 00:01:50.418
I don't know how to do this,

00:01:50.418 --> 00:01:52.695
let me look at Nick's page.

00:01:52.695 --> 00:01:54.825
That's why I do this.

00:01:54.825 --> 00:01:57.408
(upbeat music)

